# Banter in Maidenmist Cemetery (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is maidenmist_cemetery): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ mm_gate_01_rook_tobin
if name:rook_coldwake and name:tobin_hayward and at:mm_gate
interject name:rook_coldwake: That iron gate is bent outward against regulation, Tobin, and someone snapped the chain straight into the mud. Whatever left this yard did not sign the shift log.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Never mind the hinges, Rook, this mud tastes of drowned iron and lazy ditch-digging. Look at that sunken grave by the pickets, collapsing straight into the taproot.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Poor subsidence control, though the stone footing along the fence is decent enough work. Mind the turf by that unfinished rhyme, the clay has gone soft.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Half a verse carved in stone and the mason didn't even knot the end of the thought. Breathe in, man, your chest hasn't moved since the road.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Right, thank you, I had that scheduled for the gatehouse.
endif
-> END

~ mm_corpse_road_02_delphine_silas
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:silas_vane and at:mm_corpse_road
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Three miles of hearse ruts and not a single footlight on the cobbles, Silas. If this fog gets any thicker, I will have to bow to the cheap seats by ear.
interject name:silas_vane: Easy, friend, just listen to the air rattling through my ribs and keep off the verge. Every yard of this road is a marked deck of old bones.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Look at that broken hearse wheel rotting in the ditch, what a dreadful way to miss curtain. Your Foolishness is trying to rhyme "sepulcher" with "velour" and failing miserably.
interject name:silas_vane: Tell him to fold, because the chill past this worn mile marker is biting right into my knuckles. House always wins on a road built for one-way traffic.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Then let us walk faster before the damp takes the starch out of my hem.
endif
-> END

~ mm_gravestones_a_03_lucan_cordelia
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:cordelia_skein and at:mm_gravestones_a
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Hush now, the dark has teeth between these markers, Cordelia, and they are crowded in with no regard for spacing. Even Barnaby is keeping his tail tucked near my boots.
interject name:cordelia_skein: The spatial ratio is terribly cramped, though the lichen on this weathered headstone has a lovely pathology. Oh, do look, a stone with its inscription left half finished.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, what a breach of etiquette to leave a stone unfinished, and the lettering posture is three out of ten at best. Step wide of that dead tree, if you please, something is pacing the fog.
interject name:cordelia_skein: My pulse hasn't even risen, though I do admire a mason with the nerve to leave a stone half-empty.
endif
-> END

~ mm_cremation_gardens_04_silas_lucan
if name:silas_vane and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:mm_cremation_gardens
interject name:silas_vane: Ten silver says the wishing fountain is rigged, Lucan, and all these little clay urns are just waiting for a sucker to drop a coin. You feel that hum coming off the tall one?
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: That is not a wager, friend, it is a resonance, and a rather mournful specimen of pottery at that. Barnaby is staring at the purple coals in that brazier as if somebody dropped kettle corn.
interject name:silas_vane: Smart dog, at least the brazier keeps the rain off my censer while that bell tolls the count. Half these urns are dead quiet and the other half won't shut up.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Give the lavender bed its due, Silas, it masks the wet ash with admirable manners. A gentleman does not shake the urns to see who is still inside.
interject name:silas_vane: Wasn't gonna shake 'em, friend, just checking the fine print on the brick plaque.
endif
-> END

~ mm_mausoleum_lanes_05_cordelia_silas
if name:cordelia_skein and name:silas_vane and at:mm_mausoleum_lanes
interject name:cordelia_skein: Mind your ankles in the tile cracks, Silas, the viscosity of this fen-muck is positively clinging. Every vault door down the lane carries a spiral or a ship, like a taxonomy of drowning.
interject name:silas_vane: Takes me right back to the Kalero river landings, except the landlords here locked the doors from the outside. Look at that little vault sitting ajar with the hex glyph on the lintel.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Do hold still, this will only tingle while I take a silk-thread note of those pink coals by the mossy tree. The humours rising off this sunken lane are remarkably acrid.
interject name:silas_vane: Sketch fast, because my shadow is lagging a half-step in the water and it hates getting wet. Nobody carves a ship on a stone box unless they expect the tide to come up.
endif
-> END

~ mm_kings_rest_06_delphine_lucan
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:mm_kings_rest
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Now that is proper billing, Lucan, a giant stone king raising his blade right through the soup. Though the extras brawling at his rune doors could use a firmer director.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Prime specimen of royal masonry, I grant you, eight out of ten for sheer theatrical scale. Yet those wights and shrouded have been trading the same sloppy lunge for an age.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: There is broken iron everywhere and none of these fighters are even looking at the house. Why put on a show in the fog if you never take a bow?
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Because the quarry they were set to guard is long cold behind those doors, if you please. Even a loyal hound knows when to lie down after the master is gone.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Well, keep Barnaby by your heel, I have no wish to mend a spectral collar tonight.
endif
-> END

~ mm_shadestone_sanctuary_07_silas_rook
if name:silas_vane and name:rook_coldwake and at:mm_shadestone_sanctuary
interject name:silas_vane: Air's clean here, Rook, no fog pressing on the ribs and that blue fire on the ziggurat burns steady as a lighthouse. What do you make of the shovel laid flat across the slab?
interject name:rook_coldwake: Tools down, shift ended, proper and square. Whoever cut these Orc names from root to crown knew how to leave a tidy docket.
interject name:silas_vane: Look at the script on this near stone, I can almost read the stake they were marking down. Makes a bloke want to check the chalk tallies inside his own ribs.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Settle down now, Silas, a monument isn't a tab to be collected. When a stone is cut this deep, you leave the ledger as it lies and keep watch.
interject name:silas_vane: Fair enough, warden, just strange seeing a lantern statue that doesn't make my bones itch.
endif
-> END

~ mm_necropolis_depths_08_rook_cordelia
if name:rook_coldwake and name:cordelia_skein and at:mm_necropolis_depths and not flag.necrolisk_slain
interject name:rook_coldwake: Gross neglect of subterranean zoning, this, and the walls are leaking grey mist through the cracks. Whatever clawed this burrow out has no respect for load-bearing stone.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Fascinating pathology in the Shroud-ooze, Rook, see how the slime preserves the specimen in the burrow wall? My six eyes are clicking so loud I can barely hear the drips.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Keep your vials clear of it, Cordelia, my knuckles are feeling soft enough in this damp without adding cave rot. That smell is old meat and bad drainage.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Do not fret, darling, if I let this slime sour my calibration, I would be digging in the dark right alongside it. Let us clear the cavern before the ooze ruins my waistcoat.
endif
-> END
